322 - Nothing Between
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 322
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[Bb]Nothing between [F]my soul and my Savior,
[F]Naught of this world's delusive dream;
[F]I haverenounced all sinful pleasure;
[F]Jesus is mine, [Dm/F]there's [F]nothing [Am]between.

Refrain:
[F]Nothing between my [C7/Bb]soul and my Savior,
[Dm/A]so that his blessed [C7/Bb]face may be seen;
[G7/B]nothing [C]preventing [F/C]the least of his [Bb]favor;
[F]keep the way clear! let [Bb]nothing between.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Nothing between, [F]like worldly pleasure;
[F]habits of life, though harmless they seem,
[F]must not my heart from him ever sever;
[F]he is my all, [Dm/F]there's [F]nothing [Am]between.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Nothing between, [F]e'en many hard [Dm/F]trials,
[F]though the whole world against me convene;
[F]watching with prayer and much self denial,
[F]I'll triumph at last, [Dm/F]there's [F]nothing [Am]between.
